{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792320000000-review-6b-fix2.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 01:10 +07\n# Re-review round 3 (mutation method): slice 6b after fix round 2\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b`, branch `srvm-phase6b`, HEAD = `git log -1` (fix commit on a396f996). Your previous findings `collab/1792300000000-review-6b-fix1.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (F6, F7), opus's report `collab/1792310000000-engineer-6b-fix2.report.md`. Verify F6 and F7 fixed by rerunning YOUR reproductions (the if-false-ghost state completes with 73 on source and receiver, with and without the unrelated store; stripped module-store rows refuse before attach), and hunt for new defects: `live-pcs` (control-flow reachability over `analysis/successors`; closure body-pcs added; is it complete for closures constructed from reachable code, nested closures, closures held in E or store and invoked later (those are other contexts: check the context set still covers them), `:tail` states, install children); false refusals (valid states the old union rule or the previous per-context rule accepted that now refuse) and false accepts (carried free names that can run but are not discharged); the store-of census (every closure slot 4 and env slot 1, own-only per task, child vs parent same key; are there other places a store-of can hide: parked-table records, reified windows, module-store values, installing records?); portability of `live-pcs` being public. Mutants (cp backup; diff and git diff --quiet to verify restore): `live-pcs` returns only the resume pc; ignore closure body-pcs; census ignores env slot; census ignores closures inside module stores; parent census used for children; drop the new attach-count check. Say which survive. Run `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` and `-i :slow`, foreground. Findings `collab/1792320000000-review-6b-fix2.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` ending VERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE or CHANGES_REQUESTED. Edit nothing else.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
