{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1840,1900p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; cat /private/tmp/review-6b-fix2-original.log; tail -5 /private/tmp/review-6b-fix2-quick.log; rg -n 'store-of|closure|env' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives) and custody, each step over the whole tree before the\n   next, all before the first attach! (step 11); then restore (step 12),\n   which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the restored machine,\n   or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies! check-custody!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task)))))\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n:routed-store-original :attaches 1 :value 42\n:routed-store-removed :attaches 0 :refusal :yin.k/unsatisfied :value {:message \"No implementation of method: :value of protocol: #'yin.vm/IVM found for class: clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap\", :data nil}\n:past-branch {:accepted true, :module-stores 0, :source-result 73, :receiver-result 73, :attaches 1}\n:host-free #:yin.k{:status :yin.k/non-portable, :kind :host-state-primitive}\n:host-shadowed-by-E true\n:host-shadowed-by-store true\ncounterexample-search with children 20 states: {:numbered 19, :refused 1, :max-work 308801} failures: 0\ncounterexample-search incidence families 100 states: {:numbered 74, :refused 26, :max-work 421748} failures: 0\n\nRan 51 tests containing 1049 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n54:   :env [[:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n55:   :closure [:A :N :syms [:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n57:   :act [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] [:ref :k] :N]\n60:   :kframe [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] :N]\n761:(def value-row-kinds #{:vec :list :set :map :closure :prim :stream :reified :parked-ref})\n998:(defn- env-node\n1000:  (node :env [(keyed-node :bindings (:yin.k/bindings e) encode) (:yin.k/store-of e)]))\n1005:  (node :kframe [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\n1013:   :ffi-request [:yin.k/call-id :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/response-cursor-cell :yin.k/op-id]\n1014:   :link-request [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/op-id]\n1028:                 (node :act [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\n1050:(defn- decode-env\n1052:  (let [[bindings store-of] (:slots n)]\n1054:      (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))))\n1061:     :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value) :yin.k/rd rd}))\n1077:        act? (assoc :yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value))\n1097:        free-env (decode-keyed (nth slots 5) decoded-value)\n1102:        ctx {:free-env free-env :ffi-call-ids ffi-ids}]\n1135:;; stores, the free environment, the result and install children, every\n1238:  \"Record that segment a can run from pc at under environment e: a\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
